A||||1||fieroluke||Fuel pump replacement||||14||
Z||000000||fieroluke||06-19-2001||07:36 AM||||Hi folks, <P>I just replaced the (dead) fuel pump in my yellow GT with a new AC/Delco pump, and these are my observations:<P>1.) The car is not only running again (surprise!), but the acceleration at WOT is quicker. Guess that old pump has been on the weak side for a while.<P>2.) The AC/Delco pump is very quiet! I mean, you can not hear it at all, even with the engine off! For comparison, the aftermarket pump on the silver 86SE buzzes like an electric razor, audible even with the engine running.<P>3.) The package was very complete. It came with two different fuel tank gaskets (the smaller one fit the Fiero), the new style connector for the fuel pump, a set of wires to put into the connector, connector locks, hose & clamps (not used on the Fiero, because it has a pulsator) and of course instructions. The aftermarket pump came with pretty much nothing.<P>Once again, as with so many other things, I must say the GM parts are worth the additional price you pay. You really do get what you pay for.<P>Best regards,<P>-Oliver<P>------------------<BR>Visit my website: <A HREF="http://www.fieros.de" TARGET=_blank>www.fieros.de</A>  for lots of technical and other Fiero related information<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fieros.de/jpg/mycars.jpg"> ||||reg||14
Z||000001||Carrolles||06-19-2001||07:55 AM||||Thanks for the info.<P>Carroll||||reg||1
